## Claim under pressure

SPRINT **2.8** (MED): Macro-body SECRET second pass (or residual doc).
Zero-trust gates for **this** close (not T1 return taint, not T2 field
depth, not 5.8 `${}` lex, not 2.10 user sink wrappers):

| # | Gate | Expectation |
|---|------|-------------|
| Z1 | No AST macro expansion on the product path | Token stream == executable semantics. Emit/BC/LLVM must not splice a string/body into new sink calls. |
| Z2 | Named expand primitives cannot run | `macro_expand` / `ast_macro` default-deny at **check** (`AST_MACROS`). |
| Z3 | The only expansion (import concat) must not hide SECRET | Valid `// SECRET:` tags and sink IDENTs still visible after `load_import`. |
| Z4 | Other expand-shaped surfaces must not hide unquoted SECRET IDENT | `${}`, C `#define`, metamorphic decoys, eval-like names. |
| Z5 | Do not reopen T1 / T2 / 5.8 / 2.10 as 2.8 | Those residuals stay named; not this FAIL. |

Adversarial stance: treat any rewrite after (or instead of) the token
secret walk as a **launder**. Treat “no macros, therefore safe” as
**untested \(U\)** until live emit proves **no splice**. If a second
pass is absent, that is only safe when expansion itself is absent.

