---

## What we do **not** claim

- A macro-body SECRET second pass is **implemented** (it is not).
- Full IFC / `#[Secret]` / interproc beyond path A.
- `${}` interpolation (5.8) or `__sec_sink__` wrappers (2.10).
- emit-without-check is as tight as `oodac check` on residual names.
- `ooda` product CLI on out-of-tree `/tmp` paths (this host: in-tree
  `residual_path_a_floor_smoke` product refuse is the rail).

